    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="0903" n="1737" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10369</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-19T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 14, noon. Inform Department immediately by cable if the seven points
                    set forth in your June 14 were agreed to and are to be immediately acted upon by
                    the Cuban Government.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d810-f1"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0904" n="1738" xml:id="pg1738"/>
                <p>You may inform that Government that coal sent to Cuba is “for the benefit of
                    Cuba”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d810-f1" n="2" xml:id="d810-f1-content">
                <p>Answered June 19, “Yes.” (File No. 763.72/10417.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
